Dear Em Dash,

I just want to start off by saying that you’re marvelous. The aura that you add to a piece of text is commendable — whether it be an essay, a journal entry, or an email. You are the pinnacle of punctuation. Humans have adapted and created many linguistic advancements over the past millenia, yet none compare to you. 

I still recall, just about a year ago, I attempted to find fellow fans — people that adored and admired you just as much as I do. I searched to no avail, except one small blog article written almost a decade ago. I thought I was alone in truly seeing you in all your glory. It was hard for me to believe that people looked over you, that they could keep their love for you to themselves. I know I wasn’t able to — I’d talk about you to anyone who would listen.

I’m sorry about the recent negative attention you’ve been getting. It’s not your fault that ChatGPT also sees your incredible value, unfortunately weaponizing you to be its trademark. I want you to know that despite the adverse circumstances between us right now, I still treasure you. I promise I won’t leave you, and I will stand up for you if questioned by authorities. You deserve to be used the way you were meant to. I won’t let stereotypes and negative narratives separate us. Stay strong and keep your head up. This too, shall pass.

Love,
Alyssia Tan

